<title>UK: Bakyrchik Gold places shares at 200p.</title>
<headline>Bakyrchik Gold places shares at 200p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bakyrchik Gold Plc said on Friday it placed about 3.8 million new ordinary shares at 200 pence per share, raising some 7.1 million stg.</p>
<p>The share issue represented about 9.9 percent of the company's share capital.</p>
<p>The company said the shares were placed with a number of undisclosed institutions.</p>
<p>Bakyrchik's shares were marked up 3.5p at 205 by 0820 GMT.</p>
<p>Last month, the company said it planned a placing to help fund three feasibility studies on production costs and the Bakyrchik gold mine in Kazakhstan.</p>
<p>Subsequent to the placing, Bakyrchik's largest shareholder, Indochina Goldfields Ltd, owned about 11.2 million ordinary shares, representing some 27.9 percent of the enlarged share capital.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
